This project demonstrates how to train and evaluate multiple models on the MNIST handwritten digit classification task, using:
1. XGBoost 
2. Feedforward Neural Network (FNN) using Keras
3. Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) using Keras for image recognition

All models are trained using a shared interface (MnistClassifierInterface) with a common train() and predict() API.

How to Run 
1. Install required packages from requirements.txt
2. Run the script from Image_Classification_+_OOP.ipynb
You’ll see the training and validation accuracy for all three models
